  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\n\nA more defined longwave trough is projected to dig into the\nupper Great Lakes by Thursday, providing the necessary push to\ndrive the surface front southward into central Illinois. The\nboundary will likely waver across the central portion of the\nstate through Saturday before lifting northward as a warm front\nover the weekend. Deep moisture and instability laid out along\nthis boundary, combined with additional ridge-riders, will\nmaintain daily chances for showers and thunderstorms through\nSunday. The exception may be Saturday, when the upper ridge axis\nbriefly builds overhead to provide a brief lull in convective\nactivity.",
